direction: down

title: |md
  ### IPv6 extension headers
  (chain after ipv6hdr)
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

ipv6: "IPv6 base header" {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
  i_body: |md
    nexthdr field tells what's next:

    - 6 = TCP
    - 17 = UDP
    - 58 = ICMPv6
    - 0 = HOP-BY-HOP options
    - 43 = Routing header (SR, RPL)
    - 44 = Fragment header
    - 60 = Destination options
    - 50/51 = ESP/AH (IPsec)
    - 135 = Mobility (RFC 6275)
  |
}

chain: "Each ext hdr has its own nexthdr" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  c_body: |md
    Headers chain (each -> nexthdr):

    [ipv6 nh=43] ->
    [routing nh=60] ->
    [destopt nh=6] ->
    [TCP]

    - Walk via `ipv6_skip_exthdr()`
    - in `net/ipv6/exthdrs.c`
    - Each hop walks one extension
    - Some are end-host only
    - (HOPOPT processed everywhere)
  |
}

risks: "Why this matters" {
  style.fill: "#fee2e2"
  r_body: |md
    - Length-prefixed parsers
    - are bug fertile
    - (Day's homework)
    - SRv6 grew the kernel
    - many CVEs (recent fix:
    - ipv6 rpl srh OOB write,
    - kernel 7.0)
    - Each extension can grow
    - the headroom — the stack
    - must reserve mac_len for
    - re-pushed headers
  |
}

ipv6 -> chain -> risks
